{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -25 target/profile/p4-resume-chain-focused.log && rg -n '\\\\\"'^:slow|deftest'\"' test/yang/php/antlr/{objects_test.clj,class_model_test.cljc} && rg -n 'gen-content' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc | head -12 && sed -n '350,417p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc && sed -n '1,100p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"Loading initial Timbre config from: :default\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yang.php.antlr.generators-test\nREACHABLE-HEAP :ast-walker $k < 10 [151 171339]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/objects_test.clj:8:    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/objects_test.clj:28:(deftest enabled-p4-fixtures-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/objects_test.clj:40:(deftest objects-s2-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/objects_test.clj:97:(deftest checkpoint-b-typed-property-destructuring-reference-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:8:    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:84:(deftest declare-and-inherit-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:120:(deftest property-identity-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:140:(deftest static-sharing-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:161:(deftest constants-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:178:(deftest methods-and-abstracts-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:212:(deftest trait-specialization-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:269:(deftest enum-descriptor-test\ntest/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc:289:(deftest p4-registry-is-inert-test\n411:    [py/gen-content\n415:     (fn [name body] (cell/new (assoc (py/gen-content name :created) :body body)))]\n430:               (do (cell/set! g (py/gen-content (get c :name) :closed))\n447:                  (cell/set! g (assoc (assoc (py/gen-content (get c :name) :running)\n473:         (do (cell/set! g (py/gen-content (get c :name) :closed))\n492:                    (cell/set! g (assoc (assoc (py/gen-content (get c :name) :suspended)\n     (fn [x] (if (= (py/content-type x) :instance) (get (cell/get x) :class) :py/None))]\n    [py/with\n     ;; the language reference's expansion: __exit__ is looked up before\n     ;; __enter__ runs; an exception calls __exit__(type, value, None) and\n     ;; is suppressed when that is truthy; every other exit calls\n     ;; __exit__(None, None, None)\n     ;; Both dunders are looked up on the manager's type, as implicit\n     ;; invocations are; an instance attribute of that name is not used.\n     (fn [mgr suite]\n       (let [cls (py/type-of mgr)\n             enter-fn (if (= cls :py/None) :py/missing (py/class-lookup cls \"__enter__\"))\n             exit-fn (if (= cls :py/None) :py/missing (py/class-lookup cls \"__exit__\"))]\n         (if (if (= enter-fn :py/missing) true (= exit-fn :py/missing))\n           (py/type-error\n             {:py/str \"object does not support the context manager protocol\"})\n           (py/with-bound mgr (py/bind mgr enter-fn) (py/bind mgr exit-fn) suite))))]\n    [py/with-bound\n     (fn [mgr enter exit suite]\n       (let [value (py/call enter [])\n             hit (cell/new false)]\n         (py/try-finally\n           (fn []\n             (py/try (fn [] (suite value))\n                     (fn [e]\n                       (do (cell/set! hit true)\n                           (if (py/truthy\n                                 (py/call exit\n                                          (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj [] (py/type-of e)) e)\n                                                    :py/None)))\n                             :py/None\n                             (py/raise e))))\n                     (fn [] :py/None)))\n           (fn [x]\n             (if (cell/get hit)\n               :py/None\n               (py/call exit (py/vconj (py/vconj (py/vconj [] :py/None) :py/None)\n                                       :py/None)))))))]\n\n    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------- generators\n    ;; A generator is a cell holding {:py/type :generator :name s :state st}\n    ;; and the slots of its state, nothing else (every transition rebuilds\n    ;; the content, so no slot outlives its state):\n    ;;   :created    :body      (fn [g] ...), the function body\n    ;;   :suspended  :resume    the continuation captured at the yield\n    ;;               :ctx       the generator's own dynamic context\n    ;;   :running    :return    the active switch's continuation\n    ;;               :caller-ctx the switching caller's dynamic context\n    ;;   :closed     nothing\n    ;; The generator owns its dynamic context (handler stack and its\n    ;; depth relative to :base), so every snapshot the C1 forms take inside\n    ;; the body is of that record and resumes from any caller depth. Every\n    ;; crossing in sets :base to the resumer's absolute depth plus one, the\n    ;; generator's own frame, so depth measures the current continuation;\n    ;; every way back restores the caller's record whole, so no depth leaks\n    ;; across the crossing in either direction. A start or resume whose\n    ;; generator frame would exceed `py.rt/limit` is refused with\n    ;; RecursionError before anything is written. `py/gen-switch` sends\n    ;; [:send v] or [:throw e] and answers [:yield v], [:return v] or\n    ;; [:raise e]; it never raises from the generator's side. Each crossing\n    ;; restores the receiving side's dynamic context, then invokes the\n    ;; receiving continuation once.\n    [py/gen-content\n     (fn [name state]\n       (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :py/type :generator) :name name) :state state))]\n    [py/make-generator\n     (fn [name body] (cell/new (assoc (py/gen-content name :created) :body body)))]\n    [py/outcome (fn [tag v] (py/vconj (py/vconj [] tag) v))]\n    [py/gen-switch\n(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.php.antlr.quoted/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.php.antlr.prelude\n  \"The PHP runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 3.5, 7, 9). PHP semantics for operators,\n   juggling, comparison, output and errors live here as guest code, not in\n   Clojure: the lowering only emits applications of these names.\n\n   Value encoding (P1):\n     int             host integer in [-2^63, 2^63-1] (a BigInt carrier on JS\n                     past 2^53); every operator computes the exact result\n                     through the `integer` module and demotes to float when\n                     it leaves the range\n     float           untagged Jing float64 content (`data/float64`), the\n                     shared ruling of yang.typescript.md section 2; the kind\n                     test is `php/kind`, never a second tag. The prelude\n                     holds no integral float literal (JS reads 1.0 as 1):\n                     floats are built with `data/float64` or computed, and\n                     host arithmetic only ever sees `data/float-value`\n     string          a host string whose every char is one byte (a latin-1\n                     carrier); the lowering resolves literal text to bytes\n     bool            host true / false\n     null            :php/null\n     array           {:php/type :array :index {key value} :order [key ...]\n                     :next-index n}: a persistent ordered map; keys are\n                     ints or strings (`php/array-key`); `:next-index` is\n                     absent until the first integer key is written\n     error object    {:php/type :obj :class name :ord n :props {\\\"message\\\"\n                     \\\"code\\\" \\\"previous\\\"}}\n     function        a cell {:php/type :function :name s :code (fn [args])\n                             :yang.call/entry (fn [invocation])}\n\n   Runtime state is allocated by `php/init!`, once per task, under the slot\n   `php.rt/state` (the literal `:php/uninit` until `php/init!` flips it to\n   `:php/ready` as its last write):\n     php.rt/ctx            the dynamic context {:handlers :depth :base :frame}\n     php.rt/out            a cell holding the buffer stack, a vector of\n                           buffers, each a vector of byte-string chunks;\n                           `php/echo` conjs onto the last buffer, the\n                           bottom buffer is never popped\n     php.rt/globals        a cell holding the plain array of section 10.1\n                           (`$GLOBALS`), `(php/empty-array)` initially\n     php.rt/functions      a cell holding a map of lower-cased name to\n                           function cell; builtins are pre-seeded\n     php.rt/classes        a cell holding a map of class name to class record\n                           (the Throwable hierarchy, data only)\n     php.rt/next-ord       a cell, the per-task object ordinal\n     php.rt/next-cell      a cell, the per-task counted-cell id (`:id`)\n     php.rt/error-handler  a cell, :php/null or a callable\n     php.rt/error-reporting a cell, the mask (E_ALL initially)\n     php.rt/diag           a cell, the vector of diagnostic records\n     php.rt/int-max, php.rt/int-min   exact integers computed in `init!`,\n                           never literals (literals past 2^53 are not\n                           portable)\n\n   Errors are raised with `php/raise`; with no handler frame above them they\n   reach the unit root, `php/run-main`, which answers\n   `{:php/out s :php/diag [...] :php/uncaught nil-or-{:class :message}}`.\n\n   Float text: `php/float-text x ndigit` is `zend_gcvt`; `ndigit` 14 is\n   `echo` (precision), 17 is `var_dump` (serialize_precision -1, the\n   shortest round trip from `integer/float-digits`).\n\n   Two emitters, one source: `definitions` is the only definition list.\n   `uast` is the bundled prelude; `module-uast` is the same list as the\n   linker module `php`. The module emitter strips only the module's own\n   namespace `php/`; `php.rt/*` stays qualified.\n\n   Host names the prelude depends on and does not define: `host-names`.\"\n  (:require\n    #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.builtins :as builtins]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude-module :as module-defs]\n    [yang.php.antlr.quoted :refer [defquoted]]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n\n\n(def host-names\n  \"Module exports the prelude calls.\"\n  '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! data/count data/subvec data/str-concat\n     data/str-length data/str-join data/str-compare data/str->code-points\n     data/code-points->str data/substring data/float64 data/float-value\n     data/content= data/number? data/dissoc data/into\n     integer/add integer/sub integer/neg integer/mul integer/compare\n     integer/to-float integer/compare-float integer/true-div integer/pow\n     integer/shift-left integer/shift-right integer/bit-and integer/bit-or\n     integer/bit-xor integer/bit-not integer/from-float integer/quot-rem\n     integer/floor-div-mod integer/format integer/parse\n     integer/float-digits integer/decimal->float})\n\n\n(defquoted ^:private core-definitions\n  \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n  '[;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- basics\n    [php/vconj (fn [xs x] (conj xs x))]\n    [php/pair (fn [a b] (php/vconj (php/vconj [] a) b))]\n    [php/f (fn [h] (data/float64 h))]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
