{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/1793515000000-engineer-p4-leak-fix.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# PHP P4 S8 generator resume-chain retention findings\n\nBranch: \"'`yang-php-p4`; starting commit: `18ef324d`.\n\n## Requested change\n\n`php/gen-enter` now rebuilds the running state from an empty map. It keeps\n`:name`, `:cleanup`, `:current`, `:key`, and `:next-key`, installs the active\n`:return` and `:caller-ctx`, and omits `:resume`, `:ctx`, and `:body`.\nNo destructor releases were added; the corrected reachable-heap fixture and\nits equality assertion are unchanged.\n\nThe old suspended state remains the local `s` used by the same invocation to\nrestore `php.rt/ctx` and invoke `:resume`. Those are the only readers of the\nsuspension fields in the PHP runtime. Cleanup remains necessary for created\nand suspended generator destruction, so it is preserved.\n\n## Exact-scope gate result\n\nThe prescribed `gen-enter` rebuild alone does **not** close the regression.\nThe explicit slow test still fails equality on all four VMs; all eight\nsingle-suspended-`h` root checks pass. Measured values are `[live cells,\ndeep-size structural units]`, not bytes:\n\n| VM | N=10 | N=1000 |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| AST walker | 151 / 171,339 | 5,596 / 984,624 |\n| Semantic | 151 / 23,191 | 5,596 / 784,501 |\n| Stack | 151 / 131,282 | 5,596 / 701,027 |\n| Register | 151 / 444,408 | 5,596 / 1,152,753 |\n\nThe focused runner executes `clojure.test/run-tests` on the entire generators,\nobjects, and class-model namespaces, with no quick-tier exclusion. Its only\ninstrumentation wraps the existing private measurement function to print its\nreturn value; collection roots, PHP source, and assertions are untouched.\n\nCommand:\n\n```sh\nclojure -Sdeps '\"'{:aliases {:p4-gate {:extra-paths [\\\"test\\\"]}}}' \\\\\n  -M:p4-gate /private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-gate.clj\n\"'```\n\nLog: `target/profile/p4-resume-chain-focused.log`.\n\n## Remaining investigation\n\n`php/yield-raw` still copies the running state into the suspended state,\nincluding the caller'\"'s \"'`:return` and `:caller-ctx`. Also, `php/yield` keeps its\nlocal running state `s` alive across the call to `php/yield-raw`. The Python\nprelude rebuilds both running and suspended states and its yield wrapper\ndoes not hold such a state snapshot across suspension.\n\nA repository-independent, in-memory experiment is prepared at\n`/private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-diagnose.clj` to test these additional paths.\nThe user was asked whether the explicitly bounded source scope may be widened\nif this experiment proves additional changes necessary.\n\n## Validation so far\n\n- `cljstyle check src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`: passed.\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`: 0 errors,\n  0 warnings.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\nEOF\ntail -10 target/profile/p4-resume-chain-focused.log'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
